# --- Elevated review paths -------------------------------------------------
# These paths carry the highest blast radius. In a real adoption these should
# require two approvers, at least one from outside the authoring team.

# Infrastructure and deployment: a mistake here affects every service
/infra/                     @melrasheed

# Delivery controls live in workflow code. The Azure Boards release gate, the
# environment bindings that enforce production approval, and the rollback logic
# are all here — changing any of them is a governance change, not a chore.
/.github/workflows/         @melrasheed

# The release gate itself. Weakening it removes the block on shipping over a
# known Sev1 defect.
/tools/boards-gate.mjs      @melrasheed
/tools/boards-comment.mjs   @melrasheed

# The agent fleet defines how AI behaves across the whole lifecycle.
# Changing an agent definition silently changes the behaviour of every future
# AI contribution, so treat it as a governance change, not a docs change.
